course: dictionary
lesson: 13212
title: Furred
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Furred» can describe something covered in fur, or in a soft coat of hair. Look at the words around it for clues. «The furred rabbit crept out of its burrow.» A rabbit has fur, so furred means covered with fur.
explain: «Furred» can also mean lined or trimmed with fur, like a hood. «Mum wore a coat with a furred hood.» The clue is the coat and the word hood: the hood has fur on it to keep warm. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: In Britain, «furred» can mean coated with a crusty layer. «The kettle was furred up with limescale.» The clues are kettle and limescale, which build up as a crust inside. Your tongue can also be furred when you are ill.
fact: Furred is an adjective, and it is also the past form of the verb fur.
fact: «Furred» means covered with fur or a coat of soft hair.
fact: «Furred» can mean lined or trimmed with fur, like a furred hood.
fact: «Furred» can mean coated with a crusty layer, like a kettle furred with limescale.
fact: «Furred» can describe a tongue with a whitish coating when you are ill.
exercise: «The furred rabbit crept out of its burrow.» What does furred mean here? | Hidden under the bed | Made of glass | *Covered with fur | Very fast
exercise: «The kettle was furred up with limescale.» What does furred mean here? | Broken in two | Full of hot water | Shiny and clean | *Coated with a crusty layer
exercise: Which word in «Mum wore a coat with a furred hood.» tells you the hood has fur on it? | *furred | Mum | coat | wore
test: «When Sam had a fever, his tongue felt furred.» What does furred suggest about his tongue? | Bright and shiny | Cold and wet | *Covered with a whitish coating when he is ill | Very long and pink
test: Ella says «furred» means very fast. What does it really mean? | Hot and dry | *Covered with fur, or with a soft coat of hair | Very fast and quick | Lost in a forest
exam: Which sentence uses furred to mean coated with a crusty layer? | *«The kettle was furred up with limescale.» | «She wore a furred hat in the snow.» | «The cat's furred coat was soft.»
